{"id": "ych1_v1_u0_c0_pdf012_0087", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International AS/A Level Chemistry Student Book 1", "author": "Cliff Curtis, Jason Murgatroyd, David Scott", "unit_no": null, "unit_name": null, "chapter_no": null, "chapter_title": null, "section": "Procedure", "content_type": "front_matter", "book_pages": null, "pdf_pages": [12, 12], "char_count": 648, "text": "Procedure\n\n• 2 Place approximately 0.05g of calcium carbonate in a test tulbe.\n\n• 1Place 30m? of 1 mol dm? ethanoic acidin the boiling tube.\n\n• 3Weigh the test tube and its contents aocurately\n\n• 5 Once the reattion is ove,measure the volume f gas produced (as collected in a measuring cylinder)\n\n• 4Remove the bung from the boling ube and ti the calkium carbonate into the bolling tube. Quikckly replace the bung in the boilling tue.\n\nIntheStudentBook,the CorePractical specifications aresuppliedintherelevant sections.\n\nCORE PRACTICAL 1: MEASUREMENT OF THE MOLAR VOLUME OF GAS\n\nobjectives\n\n• ● To find the volume of one mole of carbon dioxide gas"}
