{"id": "ych1_v1_u0_c0_pdf012_0091", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International AS/A Level Chemistry Student Book 1", "author": "Cliff Curtis, Jason Murgatroyd, David Scott", "unit_no": null, "unit_name": null, "chapter_no": null, "chapter_title": null, "section": "Learning tips", "content_type": "front_matter", "book_pages": null, "pdf_pages": [12, 12], "char_count": 902, "text": "Learning tips\n\n• ● Keep scales simple: one large square as 5 or 10 or 20 is ideal. A scale where one lange sqguare represents 3 or 7 units or simllr) is very ifficult to plot on and this often leads to errors.\n\n• ● 50<mmoasuring cylinder\n\n• ●mass balance (2 dp)\n\n• ●Ensurethat points ploted on graph take upmore thanhalf the avilable space on each scale. Axes must ocoupy at least half f the space on the graph paper.\n\n• uβuo a Bnous o8 pnous au qde aqs aaqm Japsuo s/ewq ●\n\n• ● Straight lines should be dran with the aid of a rulelng enough to cover the full length of the line.\n\nResults (Use this space to record your results)\n\n• ●1 moldm ethanoic acid ● powdered calcium carbonate\n\n• Wear eye protection.\n\nSafety\n\n• unq a a delivery tube gets blocked, lear the bleckage and repeat the procedure from the start.\n\n• Avoid skin contact with the ethancic atid espeiallyi the skin is broken or sensitive."}
