{"id": "ych1_v1_u2_c0_pdf076_0459", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International AS/A Level Chemistry Student Book 1", "author": "Cliff Curtis, Jason Murgatroyd, David Scott", "unit_no": 2, "unit_name": "Unit 1: Structure, Bonding and Introduction to Organic Chemistry", "chapter_no": null, "chapter_title": "Topic 2: Atomic Structure and the Periodic Table", "section": "(TotalforQuestion10=6marks)", "content_type": "chapter_questions", "book_pages": [63, 63], "pdf_pages": [76, 76], "char_count": 617, "text": "(TotalforQuestion10=6marks)\n\n• 11 (a) State what is meant by an orbital.\n\n• (b) Draw the shapes of:\n\n• (i)an s-orbital\n\n• (i a p-orbital.\n\n[2]\n\n• (c) How many electrons can occupy\n\n• (i) an s-orbital\n\n• (ia p-subshell?\n\n[2]\n\n• (d) Using s and p notation, give the electronic configurations of each of the following atoms and ions:\n\n• (i)Na\n\n• (iO2-\n\n• (ii) Mg2+\n\n• (iv) Cl\n\n[4]\n\n• (e) Which of these ions contains the fewest number of electrons?\n\nA NH4+\n\nB P3- C S²- D Cl-\n\n[1]\n\n(Total for Question 11 = 11 marks)\n\n• 12 Chlorine has two isotopes, 35Cl and 37Cl. The diagram shows part of the mass spectrum of a sample"}
