{"id": "ych1_v1_u2_c0_pdf076_0461", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International AS/A Level Chemistry Student Book 1", "author": "Cliff Curtis, Jason Murgatroyd, David Scott", "unit_no": 2, "unit_name": "Unit 1: Structure, Bonding and Introduction to Organic Chemistry", "chapter_no": null, "chapter_title": "Topic 2: Atomic Structure and the Periodic Table", "section": "lonisation energy/kJmol-1", "content_type": "chapter_questions", "book_pages": [63, 63], "pdf_pages": [76, 76], "char_count": 684, "text": "Explain why:\n\n• (a) the first ionisation energy of sodium is lower than that of the first ionisation energy of magnesium.\n\n• (b) the first ionisation energy of magnesium is higher than the first ionisation energy of aluminium.\n\n• (c) the second ionisation energy of magnesium is lower than the second ionisation energy of aluminium.\n\n[2]\n\n• (d) the fourth ionisation energy of aluminium is higher than its third ionisation energy.\n\n[2]\n\n(Total for Question 13 = 8 marks)\n\n• 14Lithium isanelementin thes-blockof thePeriodicTable. Naturally occurringlithiumcontains a mixture of twoisotopes, 6Li and 7Li.\n\n• (a)Complete the table to show the atomic structure ofeach of the two isotopes."}
