{"id": "ych1_v1_u3_c9_pdf092_0545", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International AS/A Level Chemistry Student Book 1", "author": "Cliff Curtis, Jason Murgatroyd, David Scott", "unit_no": 3, "unit_name": "Unit 1: Structure, Bonding and Introduction to Organic Chemistry", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "3B Covalent bonding", "section": "DOT-AND-CROSSDIAGRAMSOFMOLECULESCONTAINING MULTIPLEBONDS", "content_type": "body", "book_pages": [79, 79], "pdf_pages": [92, 92], "char_count": 317, "text": "DOT-AND-CROSSDIAGRAMSOFMOLECULESCONTAINING MULTIPLEBONDS\n\nTable C shows the dot-and-cross diagrams for three molecules (O2, N2, CO2) that contain a double or triple bond.\n\nDISPLAYEDFORMULAE(FULLSTRUCTURALFORMULAE)\n\nA displayed (full structural) formula shows each bonding pair as alinedrawnbetweenthetwoatomsinvolved."}
{"id": "ych1_v1_u3_c9_pdf092_0547", "book_title": "Pearson Edexcel International AS/A Level Chemistry Student Book 1", "author": "Cliff Curtis, Jason Murgatroyd, David Scott", "unit_no": 3, "unit_name": "Unit 1: Structure, Bonding and Introduction to Organic Chemistry", "chapter_no": 9, "chapter_title": "3B Covalent bonding", "section": "DISPLAYEDFORMULAE(FULLSTRUCTURALFORMULAE)", "content_type": "table_data", "book_pages": [79, 79], "pdf_pages": [92, 92], "char_count": 1222, "text": "tableCExamples of displayed formulaewith thecorresponding dot-and-cross diagram.\n\n| SUBSTANCE           | DOT-AND-CROSSDIAGRAM   | DISPLAYEDFORMULA   |                                                                                            |\n|---------------------|------------------------|--------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Water, HO           | H                      | H-O-H              | LEARNINGTIP                                                                                |\n| Ammonia,NH          | H                      | H H—N-H            | Althoughit isessentialtoshow all of the non-bonding(lone) pairs of electrons in a dot-and- |\n| Oxygen, O2          |                        | O=O                | cross diagram,it isnot necessarytoshowthemina                                              |\n| Nitrogen, N2        | XNN:                   | N=N                | displayedformula.                                                                          |\n| Carbon dioxide, CO2 | :0x0o:                 | O=C=O              | SUBJECTVOCABULARY                                                                          |"}
